{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCondense 29 live prose blocks across the 11 relocated integration-test paths below. Current before-citations use origin/main@ba24f8734c922c9867645f20df35349bed885419. The original 0033662b audit established the selected anchors before the reconciler package moved. This grouped Gerrit commit also covers a nonoverlapping unit-test leaf; all path checks filter to this leaf's own 11 paths.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only ordinary comments/docstrings at the anchors below; executable statements, assertions, runtime strings, directives, and unlisted prose are immutable. Strip only leading docstrings and normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno before exact AST comparison; compare directives separately.\n\nA non-author reviewer posts one leaf-linked row per edited block:\npath<TAB>anchor/kind<TAB>before-citation<TAB>after-citation<TAB>preserved-contract-or-consumer<TAB>before-words<TAB>after-words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer-session\nUse full before/final SHAs and PASS in both verdict columns.\n\n## Scope — 29 editable blocks\n- tests/integration/reconciler/conftest.py — _default_jira_project docstring. Preserve required project value, override behavior, and cleanup.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/jira_contract/_fakes.py — module, FakeAcliClient, and install docstrings. Preserve captured shapes, deep-copy isolation, matching signatures, and the production injection seam.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/jira_contract/test_jira_fixtures.py — module docstring and comment beginning “Ticket 88d9 INVERTED…”. Preserve complementary secret scrubbing and the top-level-parent presence/falsy oracle.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/jira_contract/test_roundtrip.py — module docstring. Preserve the production-path bidirectional comment/link/parent round trip.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/jira_contract/test_snapshot_contract.py — module docstring plus docstrings of test_producer_carries_enrichment_keys and test_inbound_reads_comment_field_and_would_miss_prefix. Preserve producer/consumer shape and discriminating nested-comment/link/parent oracles.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/jira_contract/test_verified_fake_contract.py — module docstring and comment beginning “The honesty mechanism…”. Preserve shared-contract execution and the divergent-fake negative control.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/test_leaves_invocable.py — module and test_outbound_probe_leaf_genuinely_invocable docstrings. Preserve linkage versus observable invocability.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/test_link_sync.py — module and both test docstrings. Describe implemented bidirectional ADD-only link synchronization, not DESIRED/TDD/not-yet-implemented wording; retain Jira direction and representative payload shape.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/test_post_deletion_linkage.py — module docstring, comment beginning (“inbound”, “delete”)…, and test_leaves_registry_linkage_intact docstring. Preserve the surviving leaf registry and linkage-versus-invocability scope.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py — module docstring, clock comment in test_unchanged_second_pass_preserves_binding_store_bytes_and_head, and test_out_of_window_404_then_alive_roundtrip_clears_absence docstring. Preserve non-vacuous git-backed setup, lifecycle clock injection, and two-pass zero-write behavior.\n- tests/integration/reconciler/test_reconcile_roundtrip.py — module docstring, comment beginning “Ticket 4af8…”, description/oversize-description/link-roundtrip test docstrings, and comment beginning “Apply the link to the Jira snapshot…”. Preserve chained fixed-point purpose, ADF truncation protection, link direction, and no-churn/no-echo outcomes.\n\n## Consumers and protected directives\nPytest executes nine modules; conftest.py supplies fixtures; _fakes.py is imported by four jira_contract modules; scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py consumes prose. No targeted runtime documentation consumer was found.\n\nPreserve exact attachment for four directives: one # type: ignore[union-attr] in test_link_sync.py, two ignores in test_reconcile_idempotency.py (union-attr and attr-defined), and one union-attr ignore in test_reconcile_roundtrip.py.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only the 29 allowlisted blocks or adjacent blank lines change.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter.\n- [ ] Every edited block contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints.\n- [ ] Normalized ASTs exactly equal the immutable basis.\n- [ ] All four directives retain exact text and attachment.\n- [ ] Runtime strings remain AST-identical.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 11 file-impact paths.\n- [ ] The non-author TSV has one PASS/PASS row per edited block with full SHAs.\n- [ ] Every command below and every persisted structured verify command exits 0.\n\n## Verification\nRun all seven first-class DD commands using current paths and the current immutable base. The path command filters this grouped commit to this leaf's own paths.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792732572034684220,"uuid":"d8424c6e-828b-41af-82dc-f6b0e3456675"}